
I am working on the eShare Admin project for HSBC through LTIMindtree.

eShare Admin is an enterprise document management system used to manage business documents, folder structures, user access, approvals, and audit activities.

The application has two major parts. The first is eShare Admin, a web-based application used by administrators and authorized users to create and manage folders, add members, configure permissions, and assign approvers and backup approvers.

The second is the eShare client, which integrates with Windows Explorer and allows authorized users to access the configured folders and manage documents.

The system supports document operations such as check-in, check-out, and cancel check-out. It also maintains audit information about activities performed on folders and documents, which helps with traceability and accountability.

Different folder types, such as Deal, Team, Legal, Matter, and ISV, support different business requirements.

From a business perspective, the system helps organizations manage document access in a controlled manner, maintain document history and accountability, and support collaboration between authorized users.


